om global dynamics, since control hub nodes show flat ~0.88 turnover with no peak at 14476 and graph-wide unique edges decline smoothly. Population effects are excluded: displaced partners remain in the graph but stop contacting the group (0-3 events afterwards), and incoming partners pre-existed with near-zero degree. Overall activity volume is stable before and after, so the signal is a rewiring of partners, not a change in intensity or popularity."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Change point detected at t \u2248 14476\u201316500**\n\n**1. Complete contact replacement (step_02, step_03):** Group turnover rises from 0.21 \u2192 1.0, peaking at t=14476 and holding at 1.0 through t=16015, then decaying. `diff_snapshots` across the change point gives **Jaccard = 0.000** \u2014 130 edges removed, 98 added, **zero overlap**. Old cohort {55,68,118,139,441,722,788,794,901,1009,1057,1145,1444,1702,1840...} \u2192 new cohort {39,306,337,425,585,955,977,1008,1147,1181,1247,1387,1725,1734,1847...}.\n\n**2. The transition is sharp, not spread out (step_10):** Group unique edges: 20, 20, 20, 11, **0, 0, 0, 0**, 1, 29, 22. The group goes fully silent for ~2500 units and re-emerges with an entirely different partner set \u2014 a clean regime boundary rather than drift.\n\n**3. Within-regime turnover is only ~0.45 (step_13, step_14):** Before the change (4476\u21929476 vs 9476\u219214476) Jaccard = 0.449; after (16500\u219221500 vs 21500\u219226500) Jaccard = 0.474. So the group *does* have gradual background churn of ~45\u201347% per window \u2014 but the 0.0 at the change point is a categorical outlier, not the tail of that distribution.\n\n**Confounder controls:**\n- **Not activity volume (step_04):** ~84\u2013118 events per bin throughout; the group is equally active before and after. No volume spike drives the result.\n- **Not global churn (step_09, step_12):** High-activity control nodes {496,1821,318,1093,1317} show flat turnover ~0.87\u20130.92 with peak at t=5758, *not* at 14476. Graph-wide unique edges decline smoothly through the region with no discontinuity at 14476, so this is group-specific.\n- **Not node arrival/departure artifacts (step_05, step_11, step_15):** Old partners are still present in the graph but essentially never contact the group again (0\u20133 events over 13k units). New partners existed pre-change with near-zero degree (0\u20135 events over 14k units). Both sets coexist \u2014 the *wiring* switched, not the population.\n- **Not mere static connectivity (step_08):** node 865 has zero neighbours in [13900,15100], confirming a genuine temporal gap.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_c1b49572\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [323, 477, 865, 889, 1039, 1119, 1389, 1432, 1530, 1553, 1639, 1776],\n  \"window\": [246, 30246],\n  \"confidence\": 0.91,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"The group undergoes an abrupt regime switch centred near t=14476-16500. Neighbourhood turnover climbs to 1.0 and the before/after edge sets have Jaccard exactly 0.0 (130 removed, 98 added, no shared partners). The switch is sharp: group unique-edge counts fall 20->11->0 for four consecutive 500-unit bins and rebound to 29 with a wholly new partner cohort. This is distinguishable from the group's own background churn, which runs at Jaccard ~0.45-0.47 within each regime, and from global dynamics, since control hub nodes show flat ~0.88 turnover with no peak at 14476 and graph-wide unique edges decline smoothly. Population effects are excluded: displaced partners remain in the graph but stop contacting the group (0-3 events afterwards), and incoming partners pre-existed with near-zero degree. Overall activity volume is stable before and after, so the signal is a rewiring of partners, not a change in intensity or popularity.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 82199, "total_output_tokens": 5440, "total_tokens": 87639, "total_latency_ms": 91057, "llm_calls": 9, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}